- localisation/english/tank_modules_l_english.yml
- CWIC Backup/tools/validate_military_reworks.py (five regexes/format strings)

Regression risk — the one to watch: tank_special_slot_N is now the only valid slot name. Any new AI recipe, variant recipe, chassis edit, or GUI file written against special_type_slot_N will fail the validator (or silently not bind). The French and Japanese tank_modules_l_*.yml still carry 10 special_type_slot_* keys each — deliberately untouched per the English-loc-only rule, so those two languages will still show the vanilla plane titles until the translation owners update them.

3. b2cd569 — Actually patch tank designer GUI error spam

Replaced gfx/entities/zz_CWIC_armor_level0_entities.asset (313 lines, 62 aliases) with gfx/entities/zz_CWIC_armor_entity_aliases.asset (~15.2k lines, 3,019 aliases). The old file is deleted — do not resurrect it.

The previous file only covered _0 on the three base armor sub-units, so *_brigade roles and every visual level above 0 kept spamming equipment_model_util on designer hover. The new file spans base armor, tank destroyer, SP artillery, SP AA and flame sub-units across levels 0–9 (light/medium) and 0–4 (heavy), for the 75 tag/class combinations that define a base armor entity. Flame aliases clone the shared <class>_flame_tank_entity so flame art survives.

Deliberately excluded: GER light, GER heavy, ITA heavy, JAP light. The mod's units_tanks.asset replaces vanilla's and those four have no base entity to clone — they were the four Couldn't find parent clone entity errors the old file produced. The zz_ prefix is load-order critical: all existing clones in the mod resolve backward, none forward, so this must load last.

